While implementing #51, another agent was editing the MAIN working tree (not a worktree) for #29 (OTLP metrics) and #43 (Usage %{} overload). It ran git stash ("otlp-only") + git reset, which briefly wiped my uncommitted #51 changes from the working tree; they were restored when the stash was popped. The main tree is unstable: t/50_runtime_metrics_otlp.t fails 2/10 subtests and Usage.pm has been mid-edit (deep recursion / SEGV in t/98_metrics.t, t/93_to_json.t, t/90_value_objects.t during full-suite runs). Recommendation: agents editing lib/ should use isolated worktrees (EnterWorktree / git worktree) instead of the shared main tree, or coordinate stash/pop with a lock. #51 itself is verified green in an isolated worktree at the base commit (73 files, 2182 tests).
RESOLVED 2026-08-13: The SEGVs were transient — caused by karr #43's first naive %{} overload attempt (infinite recursion), not by the OTLP work. Final consolidated state (all four tickets #43/#44/#51/#41) runs 74 files / 2212 tests green, no SEGV. Recommendation stands for future parallel waves: workers must not run git stash/reset/checkout in the shared tree (Wave 2 workers are explicitly instructed to avoid all git operations).
